WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:05.305
Often said to be a silver
lining in a down market.

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:10.744
When your investments go south,

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:12.846
you can sell them from
your brokerage account

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:13.646
at a loss

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:16.750
and then use that loss
to reduce your tax bill.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:19.686
In the US, once your losses
exceed capital gains,

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:20.820
you can subtract up

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:27.761
And if your losses exceed $3,000,
that can be carried forward

00:00:27.761 --> 00:00:29.662
to offset gains in future years.

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:31.965 position:64%
That's some damage control for portfolios

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:35.802
in a bruising year in which both
stocks and bonds have declined.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:40.607
could even make the crypto
crash a little less painful.

00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:43.676
Crypto investors have collectively
lost trillions of dollars

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:48.148 position:56%
since digital coins peaked, but they
may have a special tax advantage.

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:51.484
Stock owners have to follow
what's called the wash-sale rule.

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:55.155
If they sell a stock for a loss,
they have to wait 30 days before

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:59.659 position:61%
buying the same security again, or else
it won't be eligible for a deduction.

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:04.659 position:64%
So far, the IRS has not said this
wash-sale rule applies to digital assets.

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:07.867
Still, some tax experts
warn crypto investors

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:10.303
could get burned
by the IRS'

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:12.038
economic substance doctrine.

00:01:12.038 --> 00:01:13.540
That rule basically says that

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:20.080
And if you plan on selling crypto
at a loss, make sure you know

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:22.215 position:63%
how long you've been holding your coins.

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:25.852 position:63%
Anything under the one-year mark
is considered a short-term capital loss.

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:26.820
Short-term losses

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.823
will be used to offset
short-term gains first

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:31.491
and then long-term gains.

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:35.428 position:58%
Whilst this strategy won't completely
ease the sting of crypto losses,

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:37.263
it may provide some relief.

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:38.465
Happy harvesting.

